{"step_index":867,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:16:13Z","thinking":"Nicebiz likely requires login or a paid subscription to access revenue data, preventing direct retrieval. Investigating potential Korean corporate revenue sources is required to fulfill the user's request, focusing on understanding where to obtain \"sales revenue.\" A deeper analysis is necessary to determine the reasons for mostly missing data for `24년 매출액`, and `25년 매출액` within the dataset.\n\n\nThe significant data sparsity (90%+ missing) in the revenue columns stems from the data source: CRETOP, which primarily focuses on financial data for larger entities. Korean regulations mandate public disclosure of financial statements only for \"external audit\" corporations (typically those with assets exceeding a threshold), accessible through the DART system. Smaller businesses and sole proprietorships' financial information, not subject to external audit, is considered private, and only available via paid corporate credit rating services like CRETOP, KISREPORT or ECREDIBLE. DART (Electronic Disclosure System), offers public data for a small subset, and would not contain data for a majority of the target companies.\n\n\nPublicly available data sources like the Small and Medium Business Information System, Job Portals (Saramin, Jobkorea, Catch), and the Public Procurement Service's NaraJangteo offer potential revenue data for some companies, but completeness is uncertain. The availability of 2024 and 2025 revenue data depends on the company's financial reporting timeline, with 2025 data likely being preliminary at this time. An automated test script is needed to assess the 150 companies.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Test corporate status among 150 companies","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nconst cache = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('C:/Users/lg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/22cde527-6a05-4644-ad41-9385bbc0ffd2/scratch/details_cache_150.json', 'utf8'));\n\n// Check how many are 주식회사 vs 개인\nlet corpCount = 0;\nlet indivCount = 0;\n\nfor (const [bizno, item] of Object.entries(cache)) {\n  const name = item.companyName || '';\n  if (name.includes('(주)') || name.includes('주식회사') || name.includes('(유)') || name.includes('유한회사')) {\n    corpCount++;\n  } else {\n    indivCount++;\n  }\n}\n\nconsole.log('Total:', Object.keys(cache).length);\nconsole.log('Corporations (주식회사 등):', corpCount);\nconsole.log('Individual/Other (개인 등):', indivCount);\n","Description":"Check corporation count","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\22cde527-6a05-4644-ad41-9385bbc0ffd2\\scratch\\check_corp_count.js","toolAction":"Creating check_corp_count.js","toolSummary":"Check corporation count"}}]}
